      "segment_id": "seg_amdahl_answer",
      "spoken_text": "So why does twice the computer not give you half the time? Because some part of the work can only happen one step at a time, and that part does not care how many cores you have. Twice the cores halves only the part that can be shared. A core twice as fast halves all of it.",
